cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ArchAgent: open-source public procurement tender intelligence for construction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Seyedkazemi Ardebili"
    given-names: "Mohsen"
    website: "https://mskazemi.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MSKazemi/archAgent"
url: "https://github.com/MSKazemi/archAgent"
abstract: >-
  ArchAgent is an open-source, dependency-free tender-intelligence toolkit for public-works
  procurement. It ingests notices from the TED EU Search API, scores them for fit, and applies
  a deterministic encoding of the Italian public contracts code (D.Lgs 36/2023) to derive SOA
  qualification requirements, CIG validation, provisional and definitive guarantee amounts,
  the required-document waterfall, PNRR signals, deadline urgency, and a go/no-go
  recommendation.
keywords:
  - public procurement
  - tender intelligence
  - construction
  - D.Lgs 36/2023
  - SOA qualification
  - TED
  - open data
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.5.0
